    "methods": {
      "kernel": "Same-signature temporary instrumentation in installed production IME. Real RimeBridge.key + state (up to 100 candidates) + installed EnhancedHook.update with mock processor/candidate sink. Separate Rime session, no commits. Normal and private modes; 12 fixed pinyin strings; 5 passes, first pass excluded from warm quantiles.",
      "ui": "Real production QWERTY touch injection only into local.gboard.probe. OnPreDraw samples require exact current Rime raw input and the first current candidate visible in the keyboard view tree. Three passes of four fixed pinyin strings, 183 input and 183 deletion events. Values are from injection until pre-draw; display scanout and physical touch latency excluded. Down injection waits synchronously and deliberately holds briefly, so use release-to-predraw for tap response.",
      "cold": "Two fresh production IME process launches, initialized and allowed to idle before first actual touch; no kernel/adapter prewarm. Actual first candidate predraw recorded.",
      "long_delete": "Three paired runs of a nominal 1.8-second physical delete-key hold on the same 38 ASCII letters, either Rime composition or already committed via InputConnection. Five-millisecond polling of raw composition versus editor text length. Injection acknowledgement and release allow small differences in wall duration. This is a composing-vs-committed deletion control, not an original-Gboard Chinese-engine benchmark."
    },
